# Event Loop & Asynchronous JavaScript

JavaScript is single-threaded with an event loop. Understanding microtasks vs macrotasks separates junior developers from senior candidates.

### The Execution Pipeline

1. **Call Stack**: Executes synchronous code.
2. **Microtask Queue**: Resolved Promise callbacks (`.then()`, `await`), `queueMicrotask`.
3. **Macrotask Queue**: `setTimeout`, `setInterval`, I/O, UI rendering.

> [!IMPORTANT]
> Microtasks are always drained completely before the next macrotask is processed!

### Async / Await Pattern with Clean Error Handling

```javascript
async function fetchUserData(userId) {
  try {
    const response = await fetch(`/api/users/${userId}`);
    if (!response.ok) {
      throw new Error(`HTTP error! status: ${response.status}`);
    }
    const data = await response.json();
    return data;
  } catch (err) {
    console.error('Fetch error:', err.message);
    return null;
  }
}
```

